From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] d3d10umd: indirect draws, MSAA, subroutine inlining; report feature level 11_0 (stage 4)

- Feature level 11_0 (and 10_1) is reported when the host can do it: compute and tessellation shaders, 4x MSAA
  and 8 images and shader buffers in pixel and compute shaders. The runtime asks before any device exists, so the
  adapter reads the virgl caps itself (D3DKMTEnumAdapters2, the VioGPU adapter's GET_CAPS escape).
  WINBOAT_D3D_FL11=0 reports 10_0 anyway, =1 11_0 anyway.
- DrawInstancedIndirect / DrawIndexedInstancedIndirect: D3D's argument layouts are GL's. virglrenderer ignores
  the index buffer offset in indirect draws: with one, the indices from it on are copied to a temporary buffer
  (on the GPU). Without host indirect draws (or without an index buffer) the arguments are read back.
- MSAA: quality levels, MULTISAMPLE_RENDERTARGET/LOAD, ResolveSubresource and DXGI Blt/Blt1 (resolves,
  conversions and stretches for multisampled swap chains; Blt was a stub), multisampled rasterization. The
  runtime checks the answers against each other at device creation (a typeless format and the formats it casts
  to that have MULTISAMPLE_RENDERTARGET report the same quality levels) and refused every device when they
  disagreed: sample counts are offered per format family.
- The 11.1 DDI's format caps: vertex and typed buffers, UAV writes, gather.
- call/callc: virglrenderer has no TGSI subroutines (a shader with them failed and stopped the context's
  rendering). Calls are inlined, each body in a run-once loop that ret leaves; loops and switches are looked up
  by token offset (an inlined body is translated once per call).
- Fixes found on the way:
  - D24S8 depth buffers were never created: virgl hosts only have GL's packed format (PIPE_FORMAT_S8_UINT_Z24_UNORM).
  - The pixel shader coverage input (SV_Coverage) was declared as a compute thread ID (its operand type is
    numbered among them).
---
